# Day 19 – SQL GROUP BY

## What I Learned
Today I learned about the **SQL GROUP BY clause**, which is used to group rows that have the same values in specified columns.  
`GROUP BY` is commonly used together with **aggregate functions** to summarize data.

---

## Purpose of GROUP BY
- Combine rows with the same value into a single group
- Perform calculations on each group
- Produce summarized results for analysis and reporting

---

## Basic Syntax
```sql
SELECT column_name, AGGREGATE_FUNCTION(column_name)
FROM table_name
GROUP BY column_name;
